Azure Data Factory-
- It is ETL/ELT 
-To migrate the data we can use ADF. 
Process for migration- 
Source(sql,mongodb) contains flat,csv,http files -> ADF(ETL/ELT) [iT CONTAINS CONNECTORS FOR ALL SOURCES)-> Destination(External App or cloud, AWS, DataLake.S3)
-After Extracting Data in ADF - ETL Transformation happens, for transformation  ADF has Data Flow funcationality(behind scenes it runs spark)
-Resource - It is the services that we use in Azure. Ex- Azure Data Fcatory is Resource
-Resource Groups - It is like a folder to store files.The resource that we use is stored under Resource group.
-1)Resource Azure Data Lake - We dont have Azure data lake. To get Azure ata Lake we need to do small configuration to get Azure Data Lake.We have storage accounts. By default we have azure Blob storage.
Blob storage - We can use only containers
Azure Data Lake - We can use folders inside folder( herachyial )
2)Azure Data Fctory (Resource)

Fundamental topics - 
a)Linked Service - A linked service defines the connection to a data source or an application(ADF) 
Source(sql) [Souce to ADF We need a connection(This is called Linked Service)]-> ADF-> Destination

b)DataSets- It is actual data that we need to pick, fetch or store. 
Datasets identify data within different data stores, such as tables, files, folders, and documents
Source(sql) (WE have multiple tables, To identify the table (data) which is to be migrated)-> ADF-> Destination

Practical ADF -   MIGRATE THE SOURCE Data TO Destination container
1) Create Resource Group
2) Create Resource ->First create Storage account(Microsoft storage account) 
If we want to create a data lake click on Herarcial name space button (under resource section)
3)Create Azure Data Factory 
4) Go to Resource ->storage account->create container (in data lake we create container) for souce and destination
5)upload one file in source container (use directory in data lake) 
6)Create dir and upload file inside that
7)Go to ADF studio ->Manage->Linked service-> new linked service (To establish a comnnection between source and destinationation we need a connection)
8)Copy Activity - copy data from one place to another
Process- dataset->connection->source->copy activity->sink
9)IN ADF studio create Pipeline ->copy activity -> source-> create a dataset (Data Lake gen2) and Csv file-> set properties
10)sink-> create a dataset (Data Lake gen2) and Csv file ->set properties
11) Debug this pipeline(run)

